            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great martini. For those who don't know what a lychee is, it's an asian fruit. To me, it tastes like grapefruit and pears, with the texture of a canned pear. The peach schnapps goes great with the lychee. I didn't have the white cranberry juice, so I just used all lychee juice."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "IMVINTAGE"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used 3 oz of vodka &amp; omitted the peach schnapps. I also shook it w/ crushed ice instead of cubes because it'll make the drink a bit thicker &amp; frostier using crushed ice. Took a sip &amp; then added a tsp or so of simple syrup (equal amounts sugar &amp; water boiled for a couple of minutes to dissolve the sugar...allow to cool). That not only sweetened up the drink but brought out the flavor of the lychees. Thsi went great w/ Bobby Flay's Chinese Chicken Salad...thanks for the recipe!",
            "datePublished": "2007-06-14T07:28:57.620Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Gloria Aviles"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I loved LYCHEE Martini ever since i tried it in South Beach, Miami... our variation... I blended a whole can of Lychee (puree) and used as the juice... OMG this was sooooooo awesome!!!! similar to the one at South Beach!!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-31T20:56:24.953Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RecipeRenegade"
            },
            "reviewBody": "These are quite good. I didn't have peach schnapps, so ended up adding a bit more lychee juice. This helped keep it from being too strong, as the Vodka I had on hand has quite a distinct flavor on its own. I also didn't have white cranberry juice, but used the regular red kind. It ended up a nice light pink color.\n\nI think I might try this with gin, by adding a bit of lychee juice to a gin and tonic, and adding a lychee for garnish.",
            "datePublished": "2008-06-03T20:15:24.597Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Screamer"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was the favorite among the various martinis we tried. I substituted Patrons Citronge for peach schnapps, and red cranberry instead of white cranberry - this gave nice rose tint to the drink. I also garnished it with a mint leaf. Excellent!",
            "datePublished": "2010-08-28T10:26:07.450Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Khristin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This are yummy, but very strong. I added an extra half shot of cranberry juice and a little grenadine to tone it down. I highly recommend!",
            "datePublished": "2008-04-17T06:21:36.020Z"
          },
